<title>ISRAEL: ISRAEL FUND RAISES $15 MLN FROM AT&amp;T PENSION FUND.</title>
<headline>ISRAEL FUND RAISES $15 MLN FROM AT&amp;T PENSION FUND.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israeli venture capital fund Kardan Technology Ventures said on Thursday it raised $40 million in its first round of fundraising, including $15 million from the pension fund of AT&amp;T.</p>
<p>The Israeli fund, which was established by Kardan Technologies, plans to raise a total of $75 million.</p>
<p>Another fund set up by Kardan called Nitzanim has brought two companies to Nasdaq -- ESC Medical Systems Ltd and Galileo Technology Ltd.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
